# StudentStack — Cursor Rules (strict)

## Brand & UI/UX
- Visual language: extreme modern roundness (large border radii), bubbly rounded sans-serif typography, soft and vibrant pastels, thick drop shadows, playful bouncy hover animations (reference: Duolingo, Kalshi energy).
- Interactions: prefer `motion` / CSS transitions with subtle scale and shadow on hover; avoid flat static panels without feedback.

## Icons
- Never use generic placeholder icons, emoji-as-icons for UI chrome, or “AI JSON” / stock robot icons.
- Use **Lucide React** (or other curated SVG icon libraries) or intentional **CSS shapes** only.

## Product & Content Boundaries
- **Primary product:** StudentStack Elite, a paid student portal for high schoolers.
- Landing CTA: **Apply for Elite** (parent application). Do not lead with newsletter signup.
- Portal modules: **AI Toolkit**, **Super Opportunity & Admissions Vault**, **Organization-issued AI Certifications**.
- Student login is for Elite members (credentials issued after Stripe subscription / invite).
- Present as a **student-led organization**. Do not market “AI writes everything” on the public site; portal may include an AI refresh desk for members.
- Do not feature an operator/newsletter studio on the marketing site.

## Engineering defaults
- App is Next.js under `src/`. Portal lives at `/portal`. Stripe Elite checkout/webhook under `src/app/api/stripe/`.
